meta {
  name: save one operator setting
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/settings/env
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "SPECTRO_HUB_ENABLED",
    "value": "true"
  }
}

docs {
  Write one named setting into ~/.spectro/.env (0600): SPECTRO_HUB_ENABLED (true or false; on, off, yes, no, 1 and 0 are saved as true or false), SPECTRO_HUB_PORT (blank, 0, or 1024 to 65535 except 8080 to 8100 and this server's own port) or SPECTRO_ALLOW_SPAWN (true or false). 404 for a refused caller, 400 for an unknown name or a value that is not the shape that name takes, with reason (under-1024, app-range, server-port, not-a-port, not-a-switch) and message. One locked write to a temporary file, moved over the old one: every other line of the file is kept, and an unset hub setting is left as a commented default line (# SPECTRO_HUB_ENABLED=false, # SPECTRO_HUB_PORT=7700), once.
  
  Body: {name, value}, one setting per call.
  
  CAUTION: Writes ~/.spectro/.env. Only names on the writable allow-list are accepted.
  
  Fence: host+origin+json. Loopback fence plus Origin check, and the request must carry Content-Type: application/json — anything else is 415.
  
  Writes state: yes
}
